      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sanctions are a necessary tool to pressure authoritarian regimes into respecting human rights and international law, even if they come with economic costs. While critics argue they hurt civilians, the alternative of doing nothing allows dictators to continue oppressing their own people with impunity. Real diplomacy is often impossible when a government refuses to engage, so targeted sanctions remain the only effective way to force change.",
      "source": "target",
